---
kind: lore
id: perseids
title: Counting meteors on the roof
---

// The engine raises `shower` each time a meteor goes over while the player is
// on the roof with Sol under a clear sky, with the running count as payload.
// The `holds(at(sol, roof))` guards restate the occasion's own raisedWhen:
// without them W-CAST-ABSENT fires on every Sol line.

<beat id="record" on="shower" title="A record count" priority="10" once="run" when="occasion.payload.count >= 60 && holds('at', ['sol', 'roof'])">
  @sol{emotion="laughing"}: {{occasion.payload.count}}! That beats my father's page in the '98 log. Write it down. No — I'll write it down. You'll round.
  ::set{run.aff.sol += 1}
</beat>

<beat id="tally" on="shower" title="Another one" once="false" when="holds('at', ['sol', 'roof'])">
  @sol{emotion="fond" when="occasion.payload.count == 1"}: That's one. Say a number every time.
  @sol{emotion="happy" when="occasion.payload.count > 1"}: {{occasion.payload.count:plural(# meteor|# meteors)}}. Keep going.
</beat>
